    "source_answer": "B",
    "previous_model_response": "Let \\(D\\) be the foot of the perpendicular from center \\(O\\) to chord \\(BC\\). The inscribed angle is\n\n\\[\n\\angle BAC=60^\\circ,\n\\]\n\nso the corresponding central angle is\n\n\\[\n\\angle BOC=120^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(OD\\perp BC\\), it bisects \\(\\angle BOC\\), giving \\(\\angle BOD=60^\\circ\\). In right triangle \\(BOD\\),\n\n\\[\nOD=OB\\cos60^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nGiven \\(OD=2\\),\n\n\\[\nOB=\\frac{2}{\\cos60^\\circ}=4.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\nBC=2\\cdot OB\\sin60^\\circ\n=2\\cdot4\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\n=4\\sqrt3.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D."
  },
